wayland backend: closing the window asks, rather than tears down

With KRETRO_WESTON_CLOSE_FD=N (a connected socket), closing the window -
the frame's close button, or the host's xdg_toplevel.close (Alt+F4, the
window menu) - sends one byte on socket N and leaves the window as it
is. kretro then asks the game to quit, as closing it on Windows would. A
game that is killed by its screen going away never writes what it keeps
until it exits, a player profile for one.

When the socket's reader has gone, or the variable is unset, the window
closes as upstream: the output is destroyed, and with the last one the
compositor exits.

